# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# An ALLOWLIST, not a deny list, and that is the point.
#
# A deny list sends everything it forgot. This tree is a working checkout: it
# carries a multi-gigabyte `target/`, a `node_modules/`, sibling git worktrees
# under `.claude/`, and — the reason this file is shaped this way — untracked
# personal documents the owner keeps beside the source. A build context is
# copied into the daemon and a `COPY . .` puts it in an image layer, so a deny
# list that misses one of those publishes it.
#
# So: exclude everything, then name what the two Dockerfiles actually need. A
# new directory is excluded by default and the build fails loudly when it is
# required, which is the safe direction.
*

# The workspace: `cargo build --locked` needs the manifests, the lock, the
# toolchain pin, every path dependency, and the relay itself.
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!crates/
!server/

# The editor build (`webapp/build.sh`): the webapp, the published package the
# embedding generator reads, `docs/` for the reference pages and
# `docs/assets/editor.jpg`, and the two fixtures the script stages as demos.
!webapp/
!packages/
!docs/
!fixtures/
!sample.docx

# The static-server configuration the editor image copies.
!deploy/

# Re-excluded inside the allowed trees: build output, dependencies and test
# artefacts. All of it is produced by the builder stages, and copying a host
# `target/` in would both bloat the context and invalidate every cache layer.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.DS_Store
webapp/pkg/
webapp/test-results/
webapp/playwright-report/
